# Heavy triple-barrel artillery: the first weapon in the catalog that empties EVERY barrel on
# one trigger pull (muzzle_pattern salvo), so its 20-damage shells land as a 60-damage volley
# for a single 28-point charge. Tuned against longlance_rail, the other tier-2 alpha piece:
# identical DPS (36), a third more alpha, but a third of the reach and slightly worse damage
# per capacitor -- it has to be flown into knife range to be worth mounting. Three separate
# shells also make it the only ballistic that SATURATES point defense: PD must burn down all
# three, and each is tougher than a gauss shell.
#
# Deliberately size M, not L. The only hull with authored hardpoints (assets/ships/ship/ship.ship)
# has three MEDIUM weapon slots and no large one, so an L weapon cannot be mounted anywhere in
# the game today -- see longlance_rail, which currently cannot.
id          trident_mk1
name        "Trident Siege Battery"
kind        ballistic
size        M
icon        ic-cannon
damage      20
fire_rate   0.6
proj_speed  8500
# Uniform 0.15 range compression (see autocannon_mk1): 15 -> 2.25s, 127,500 -> 19,125 units.
# The factor is shared with longlance_rail precisely so the "a third of the reach" trade
# stated above stays exactly true.
proj_life   2.25
proj_radius 5.5
cap_cost    28
emission    0.85
proj_hp     1.5
price       1500
tier        2
desc "Three barrels, one trigger, one charge. It spends most of a fight silent and the rest of it rearranging somebody's hull - but the range band where it can do that is short enough to be a decision."

# Shares the triple-barrel art with autocannon_mk1; the geometry is in hardpoint half-extents,
# so the same numbers scale correctly on any slot size.
mount_art       assets/weapons/assets/tier_1_cannon_triple_barrel.png
mount_art_size  1.95 3.00
mount_art_pivot -0.37

# All three barrels at once -- the salvo IS the weapon, and the stat block above is balanced
# around a 3-shell volley rather than a single shell.
muzzle -0.50 1.85
muzzle  0.00 1.85
muzzle  0.50 1.85
muzzle_pattern salvo
